          %p
            The general concept of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/renormalization"} renormalization
            is really important here. The universality classes we understand best correspond to fixed points of renormalization-group transforms.
          %p
            The first column, “stable distributions”, basically comes from the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/central+limit+theorem"} central limit theorem
            and the ways in which the conditions necessary for it to apply can fail to obtain. The middle column with all the funny symbols comes from
            = succeed "\u2018s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%C3%89lie+Cartan"} Élie Cartan
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+space"} symmetric spaces
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equilibrium"} equilibrium
            statistical systems can be given a taxonomy based on the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ADE+classification"} ADE classification
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dynkin+diagram"} Dynkin diagrams
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/conformal+field+theories"} conformal field theories
            %a{:href => "#Cardy2010"} Cardy 2010
            writes:
          .standout
            %p
              [T]he study of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/representation+theory"} representation theory
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Virasoro+algebra"} Virasoro algebra
              gives a way of classifying all possible
              = succeed "s" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/CFT"} CFT
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi c
                      %mo &lt;
                      %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c \lt 1
