              %tr
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"} 1977
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"} Hohenberg, Halperin
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"} Classification of critical phenomena in dynamic continuum theories
              %tr
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"} 1978–80
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"} Grassberger, Sundermeyer, de la Torre, Cardy, Sugar
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                  Connection of
                  %span.newWikiWord
                    Reggeon field theory
                    %a{:href => "/nlab/new/Reggeon+field+theory"} ?
                  with directed percolation
              %tr
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"} 1980
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                  Libchaber
                  %em et al.
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"} Observation of Feigenbaum’s constants in experimental systems, starting with convection of mercury
              %tr
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"} 1981–82
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"} Janssen, Grassberger
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"} Formulation of DP conjecture, setting out the likely criteria for phase transitions to belong to the directed-percolation class
              %tr
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"} 1984
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"} Belavin, Polyakov, Zamolodchikov
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/conformal+field+theory"} conformal field theory
                  in 2D
              %tr
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"} 1986
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"} Zamolodchikov
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/c-theorem"} c-theorem
                  for 2D theories, identifying RG fixed points with CFTs of specific
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Virasoro+algebra"} central charges
              %tr
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"} 1986
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"} Kardar, Parisi, Zhang
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"} KPZ equation for dynamical surface growth by deposition, showing that RG is applicable to its far-from-equilibrium dynamics
              %tr
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"} 1996–97
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"} Zirnbauer, Altland
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                  Symmetry classes (not
                  %em exactly
                  the same thing as universality classes, but clearly part of the same picture) for random matrices, following Cartan’s classification of symmetric spaces
              %tr
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"} 1998–99
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                  Freedman,
                  %em et al.
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                  First indications that the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/AdS%2FCFT+correspondence"} AdS/CFT correspondence
                  and related implementations of gauge/gravity duality could lead to a “holographic
                  = succeed "-theorem\u201D" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi c
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c
